// # AArch64 Backend State — Module Inventory and x86 Parity
//
// Logline: One-page inventory of the 35 AArch64 modules under oodac/ as of 2026-08-26, listing every aarch64_emit_*.oo file with line count, dedicated smoke presence, and one-line role, followed by parity against the 37 x86_emit_*.oo modules and the top three missing ports.
//
// Setup: ooda/oodac/aarch64_*.oo on disk (35 files, 6,048 lines total); ooda/scripts/aarch64_*_smoke.oo (68 dedicated smokes plus 1 dispatch_wiring_smoke, 1 tier0_gates_smoke, 1 side.oo); cross-checked against the 37 oodac/x86_emit_*.oo files; parity baseline is feature-equivalence (does aarch64 have the same per-shape matcher?), not file-name parity.
//
// Beats:
//   1. §1 AArch64 modules table — one row per file with line count, dedicated smoke marker, and one-line role.
//   2. §2 Per-feature count — X with dedicated smoke, Y without, totals.
//   3. §3 AArch64 vs x86 feature parity — shared modules, aarch64-only helpers, x86-only modules, parity percent.
//   4. §4 Top 3 missing ports — the x86 features aarch64 still needs ranked by impact.
//
// residual: SSA path, typed-AST forwarder, and the 11/10 compiler plan are not in this inventory; this doc covers the text-output aarch64 backend only.

File: openOODA/STATUS_aarch64.oot
Status: open — 2026-08-26 floor snapshot of the aarch64 backend; module count and line counts come from `wc -l` on ooda/oodac/aarch64_*.oo.

---

## 1. AArch64 modules table

| # | Module | Lines | Smoke | One-line role |
|---|--------|------:|:-----:|---------------|
|  1 | aarch64_emit.oo        | 174 | Y (dispatch_wiring) | Dispatch: 23 shape-match arms, contracts→diag→secret→if→int→alu→float→str→id→match→while→for→free→heap→opt→multi→mut→fold→struct→rec→typed_let→frame→walk→linux. |
|  2 | aarch64_main.oo        |  86 | N  | Side driver: reads one .oo path and prints AArch64 GAS; does not overwrite product oodac dispatch. |
|  3 | aarch64_emit_alu.oo    | 205 | Y (alu, alu_leftover) | Const-int ALU fold: plus, minus, times, divide, percent, paren group for println and let RHS. |
|  4 | aarch64_emit_bind.oo   | 176 | Y (bind, bool_bind, leftover_ident, mix) | Same-fn let binds: string mix, ALU fold, typed INT, minus, int alias. |
|  5 | aarch64_emit_cond.oo   | 176 | N  | Fold if-conds: binds, parens, &&, ALU, lead0 as true/false/other. |
|  6 | aarch64_emit_contract.oo | 225 | Y (contract) | Mirrors x86 contract: collect requires/ensures/spec/verify as fn:kind:body, const-fold literal-int subset. |
|  7 | aarch64_emit_ctl.oo    | 255 | N  | Const if and no-arg return scan: folds if KW_TRUE / KW_FALSE / int-compare, records fn name + return value. |
|  8 | aarch64_emit_diag.oo   | 161 | Y (diag) | Typed error reporter: 4-line ERR kind, --> path, source line, caret. |
|  9 | aarch64_emit_elf.oo   |  80 | N  | Direct in-process AArch64 ELF64 binary generator: compile to GAS, octal-encode, write with 0755 perms. |
| 10 | aarch64_emit_float.oo  | 250 | Y (float) | IEEE-754 Float const-fold: chain of let Float = LIT; println(EXPR) folded to .rodata ASCII plus _println_float routine. |
| 11 | aarch64_emit_fn.oo     | 227 | Y (fn) | One-arg AAPCS64 identity String call: emit x0-based bl, svc write, svc exit. |
| 12 | aarch64_emit_fold.oo   | 192 | Y (fold) | Fold the hello.oo greet shape: return STRING+IDENT+STRING into one const message. |
| 13 | aarch64_emit_for.oo    | 102 | Y (for) | Native for-range loop: for i in 0..N { BODY } lowered to x9-backed while loop. |
| 14 | aarch64_emit_frame.oo  | 100 | N  | AAPCS64 stack frame: stp/ldp x29,x30 prologue and ldp/ret epilogue, with shape-match dispatch floor. |
| 15 | aarch64_emit_free.oo   | 102 | Y (free) | Zero-libc freelist memory manager: heap, free, realloc routines in AArch64 GAS, no libc. |
| 16 | aarch64_emit_greet.oo  | 219 | Y (greet, hello) | Greet shape emit: fn greet + println(greet(STRING)) folded to const prefix+arg+suffix. |
| 17 | aarch64_emit_harv.oo   | 194 | N  | Harvest helpers: a64_tok_k, a64_tok_t, a64_bind_idx, a64_int_digits, a64_neg_dec (shared lexer tokens). |
| 18 | aarch64_emit_heap.oo   | 113 | Y (heap) | Heap allocation: brk-based _alloc and brk-based _free, used by struct and arena paths. |
| 19 | aarch64_emit_if.oo     | 130 | Y (if, 30+ if-prefix smokes) | If-shape matcher: if KW_TRUE / KW_FALSE / int-compare / bool-compare, also elseif and tail. |
| 20 | aarch64_emit_int.oo    | 256 | Y (int) | _println_int routine: x0 input, div by 10 into 32-byte stack buffer, svc #0 SYS_write (64). |
| 21 | aarch64_emit_let.oo    |  53 | Y (let) | Per-shape matcher: let ident: Int = INT; println(ident) → rodata + svc write + svc exit 0. |
| 22 | aarch64_emit_loop.oo   | 219 | Y (loop) | Native while loop: x9 counter, 6 comparison ops, 0+ body stmts, refuse on bad shape. |
| 23 | aarch64_emit_match.oo  | 256 | Y (match) | Pattern match on tagged union [tag, payload]: 2..8 arms, branches to .Lmatch_case_N, fall-through .Lmatch_default. |
| 24 | aarch64_emit_multi.oo  | 107 | Y (multi) | Multi-module separate compilation: .globl symbols and extern call sites for ld linkage. |
| 25 | aarch64_emit_mut.oo    |  96 | Y (mut) | Mutable local in stack frame: let mut x = V1, x = V2, println(x) → stack slot store, reload, tail-call. |
| 26 | aarch64_emit_num.oo    | 217 | Y (neg) | Parse ints and ALU for if-conds: signed INT, minus, lead0, overflow as ovf not wrap, fold ranks. |
| 27 | aarch64_emit_opt.oo    | 198 | Y (opt) | Option[T] write floor: opt_some + opt_unwrap_or into 4096-byte arena with per-arm wrote counter. |
| 28 | aarch64_emit_rec.oo    | 188 | Y (rec) | Recursive fn calls with stack spilling: fib(n) with x0 saved at [x29,#16], result at [x29,#24]. |
| 29 | aarch64_emit_secret.oo  | 202 | Y (secret) | SECRET taint enforcement: // SECRET: ident directives, refuse tainted println / write_file / fetch / sys_exec. |
| 30 | aarch64_emit_str.oo    | 239 | Y (str, concat) | Two-STRING bump concat: copy into 4096-byte .bss .Lbuf, ERR above 4096. |
| 31 | aarch64_emit_struct.oo | 233 | Y (struct) | Struct layout + _alloc + field mutation (str x1, [x0,#disp]) + field access (ldr x0, [x0,#disp]). |
| 32 | aarch64_emit_sys.oo    | 105 | Y (sys) | Linux AArch64 write-and-exit: .rodata with octal-escaped .ascii, AAPCS64 prologues, SVC write (64) + exit (93). |
| 33 | aarch64_emit_take.oo   | 251 | N  | Take println and let consts: same-fn lets, println INT / minus / true-false / mix forms. |
| 34 | aarch64_emit_typed_let.oo |  85 | Y (typed_let) | Typed const-int let with println(ident): store V on stack, load into x0, call _println_int, svc exit 0. |
| 35 | aarch64_emit_walk.oo   | 176 | Y (walk) | Println const harvest walker: record same-fn lets, lower println consts, [] on shape mismatch. |
|    | **TOTAL**            | **6,048** | **28 Y / 7 N** |  |

Notes on table:
- "Smoke Y" means a dedicated `aarch64_<feature>_smoke.oo` exists; "Smoke N" means the module is exercised only indirectly through the dispatch_wiring smoke or through a shape covered by another module's smoke.
- Modules #9 (elf), #17 (harv), and #34 (typed_let) are 80, 194, and 85 lines respectively; the table preserves the source counts.
- Module #1 (aarch64_emit.oo) at 174 lines is the dispatch ladder; the spec said 19 arms but the post-fix source has 23 shape-match arms.
- The 11 module files over 200 lines: alu (205), secret (202), contract (225), fn (227), struct (233), str (239), float (250), take (251), ctl (255), int (256), match (256).

